      "writtenOn": "2025-02-24T16:59:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This updates the shared `snk_path_en_mask` evertime this is called.  What about making `snk_path_en_mask` atomic and always modifying it everytime `port.sink_path-en` changes?\n\nAlso, in keeping with some other cleanup you should add a new variable `sink_path_status` that tracks the `status-\u003esink_path_status` returned by the PDC in the connector status message.\n\n`sink_path_en` should only be used as temporary storage when queueing the SET_SINK_PATH command.\n\nThis should be done as a separate CL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2019,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2023,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "708e141144421d98268a8d10d3a013776c6054af",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42df8c40_d5470b88",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2023,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-25T03:14:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally, I\u0027d like one source of truth of this. The `sink_path_en` is modified in 7 places within this file, with queuing the command in 6 of these instances.  I can create a helper function to update the `snk_path_en_mask` and `sink_path_en`.  \n\nI can also opt to not use the mask and return a count, I found the mask mainly helpful for debug logging purposes.",
      "parentUuid": "9e9d4d77_c1018976",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2019,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2023,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "708e141144421d98268a8d10d3a013776c6054af",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bfc0a3ef_ff00f8fa",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2023,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-25T17:56:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To clarify my earlier comment - can you add a new field to `struct pdc_port_t` to track the `sink_path_status`.  This field should reflect what we believe the current sink path state as setup by the PDC.  The field `sink_path_en` should only represent what we want to send to the PDC as part of `CMD_PDC_SET_SINK_PATH`.\n\nI believe there is a potential hole in the current implementation. the SNK ATTACHED state queries the charge manager to set `sink_path_en`, but if the PDC sends us a new connector status message before we process the `SET_SINK_PATH` command, we might overwrite `sink_path_en`.",
      "parentUuid": "42df8c40_d5470b88",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2019,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2023,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "708e141144421d98268a8d10d3a013776c6054af",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
